rem Divisibility of factorials
rem https://projecteuler.net/problem=549

use numbers
use sequences
use io
use cli

option N integer = 100000000

rem s(n) is the largest t(p, a) over
rem the p^a || n, t(p, a) the least m
rem with v_p(m!) >= a. For a = 1 that
rem is p, so start from the largest
rem prime factor (primes in order, each
rem overwriting its multiples), then
rem raise multiples of p^a, a >= 2.
S = array shape (N + 1) fill 0
for P in primes to N
  S (P to N by P) = P
end
Rt = N isqrt
Ps = primes to Rt array
Z1 = array shape 0 fill 0
Pa = Z1
Ea = Z1
for A in 2 to 30
  Pk = Ps ((Ps ** A at most N) indices)
  Pa = concat Pa Pk
  Ea = concat Ea (Pk * 0 + A)
end
rem t by bisection on Legendre's sum.
Lo = Pa * 0 + 1
Hi = Pa * Ea
for It in 1 to 40
  Md = (Lo + Hi) // 2
  V = Md * 0
  Q = Pa
  for J in 1 to 30
    V += Md // Q
    Q = Q * Pa
  end
  G = V at least Ea
  Hi = G choose Md Hi
  Lo = G choose Lo (Md + 1)
end
T = Hi
for I in 0 till Pa len
  Q = (Pa I) ** (Ea I)
  Sl = Q to N by Q
  Ti = T I
  S Sl = (S Sl) max Ti
end
Answer = (S (2 to N)) sum
Answer print
